course: dictionary
lesson: 11773
title: One word, many meanings: bats
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, so look at the words around it. Bats is a good example. «The bats flew out of the cave at dusk.» Flying animals come out at dusk, so here bats means animals.
explain: As a verb, bats means taking a turn to hit the ball in cricket. «Ravi bats next, so he will face the first ball.» The sentence is about a turn in a game, so bats means takes a turn at hitting.
explain: The informal meaning is different again. «Dad said, you must be bats to swim in that cold lake!» Dad is not talking about animals or sticks. He means you are a bit crazy. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: if it still makes sense, you have found it.
fact: Bats is the plural of bat, which means more than one bat.
fact: A bat can be a flying animal, or a wooden stick used to hit a ball in games such as cricket.
fact: As a verb, «bats» means taking a turn to hit the ball.
fact: Many bats eat thousands of insects in one night, which helps farmers.
fact: In informal British talk, «bats» means a bit crazy, as in «go bats» or «bats in the belfry».
exercise: «The bats flew out of the cave as the sun went down.» What are the bats here? | *Flying animals | Trees | Cricket sticks | Crazy people
exercise: «Ravi bats next, so he will face the first ball.» What does bats mean here? | Is a little crazy | Flies around the field | Sleeps all day | *Takes a turn hitting the ball
exercise: «Dad said you must be bats to climb that tree in the rain!» What does bats mean? | Flying in a group | Hanging upside down in the dark | *A bit crazy, in an informal way | Full of fruit
test: «Fruit bats eat fruit, and they live in groups called colonies.» In this sentence, bats means: | Sports players | *Flying animals | Cricket equipment | A bit crazy
test: «Our team kept three bats in the kit bag for the match.» What does bats mean? | To take a turn | Crazy people | Flying animals | *Sports sticks for hitting a ball
exam: «The bats came out at dusk to hunt for insects.» Which word is the best clue that bats means animals? | came | out | *insects | dusk
